"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the new group/subgroup to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a validation requirement without specifying what happens when no name or a blank/invalid name is provided, and passive voice ('to be created') omits the responsible actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-008\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A subgroup cannot be created when no group is selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify the system's response when subgroup creation is attempted with no group selected (e.g., disabling the action vs. displaying an error message), and passive voice omits the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-009\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the group/subgroup to be renamed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a validation requirement without specifying what happens if the name is empty or invalid during renaming, and passive voice ('to be renamed') omits the responsible actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"find something in a group a word\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'something' is vague and does not specify which entities or fields are searched, and 'a word' leaves unclear whether partial substrings, spaces, or special characters are permitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In order to find something in a group a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits what happens when a search is triggered with an empty find field or when no matching items exist, and passive voice ('must be placed') omits the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The attachment of 'to be created' is syntactically and temporally ambiguous: it could mean a group must already exist/be selected before creating an entry, an entry must be assigned to a group upon creation, or a group requires an entry to be created.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior if entry creation is attempted when no group exists or is selected, and passive voice ('to be created') omits the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-012\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is completed the repeat password field must be completed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a form validation rule without specifying what happens if the repeat password field is left blank (e.g., error message or blocked save), and omits the actor and applicable dialog context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Password field and repeat password field must be identical\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies a validation rule without defining the system's error handling when the password and repeat password fields do not match.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must be selected to be viewed or modified\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if viewing or modifying is attempted with no entry selected (e.g., disabled controls vs. error prompt), and passive voice omits the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is changed the repeat password field must be Changed and be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits what happens when the password field is modified but the repeat password field is not updated or does not match, and passive voice omits the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is changed the repeat password field must be Changed and be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-012\",\n        \"KP-013\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Repeats the identical-fields validation already stated unconditionally in KP-013 and near-duplicates the repeat-password completion rule in KP-012 without defining a distinct operational context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-016\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must be selected before it is duplicated\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if duplication is attempted when no entry is selected, and passive voice ('must be selected', 'is duplicated') omits the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-017\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"For the following features, use cases are not included\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The demonstrative phrase 'the following features' is fused onto the requirement without defining which features it refers to or where its scope ends.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-017\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An internet connection and a browser are required in order to download new language translations For the following features, use cases are not included\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies external dependencies (internet connection and browser) without defining behavior when offline, when no browser is available, or when a download fails; also omits the actor/download source and explicitly notes missing use cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-018\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The prefix “Auto-Type:” is required in front of each sequence\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies a syntax validation rule without defining what happens when the 'Auto-Type:' prefix is missing or malformed (e.g., ignored vs. error), and omits where sequences are entered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-019\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Sequence’s length must not be more than a line (59 characters)\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies a maximum length constraint without stating what happens if a sequence exceeds 59 characters (e.g., rejected, truncated, or ignored) or whether the 'Auto-Type:' prefix counts toward the 59-character limit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-020\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If two auto-types are referred in one note field, only the first is used\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Addresses only the case of exactly two auto-types in a note field without specifying behavior when three or more are present or whether any warning is given for ignored entries.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-020\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"auto-types\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-018\",\n        \"KP-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Switches terminology from 'sequence' / 'Sequence' (with prefix 'Auto-Type:') in KP-018 and KP-019 to 'auto-types' for the same domain concept.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-021\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Only one database file is allowed in command line options\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a command-line validation constraint without specifying system behavior when multiple database files are passed (e.g., abort with an error message vs. open only the first file).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-021\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"database file\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Refers to the KeePass database as a 'database file', whereas KP-003 refers to the '.kdb' database file as a 'Folder'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-022\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In case a space is found in the path, it must be enclosed into quotes\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The pronoun 'it' has two plausible antecedents: 'a space' or 'the path'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"it must be enclosed into quotes\",\n      \"related_id